### Phase 2: Tenant Resolution Middleware (Days 7–9)

> Wire up subdomain → tenant resolution. Existing Happy Church users must be unaffected.

- [ ] **2.1** Create `app/Http/Middleware/IdentifyTenant.php`:
  - Extract subdomain slug from request host
  - Look up `Tenant` by `slug` OR `domain` (custom domain support)
  - Abort 404 if no tenant found (except for `www.` and `admin.` subdomains)
  - Bind tenant to service container: `app()->instance('tenant', $tenant)`
  - Set `config('app.tenant_id', $tenant->id)`
- [ ] **2.2** Create `app/Http/Middleware/EnsureTenantActive.php`:
  - Check `$tenant->status` is `active` or `trial`
  - Check trial not expired: `$tenant->trial_ends_at > now()`
  - Redirect to billing/upgrade page if expired
- [ ] **2.3** Create `app/Http/Middleware/CheckModule.php`:
  - Read module name from middleware parameter: `middleware('module:finance')`
  - Use `ModuleService::isEnabled()` to check
  - Return 403 with upgrade prompt if module is off
- [ ] **2.4** Register all three middleware in [app/Http/Kernel.php](file:///Users/bien/Downloads/pisti-app/app/Http/Kernel.php)
- [ ] **2.5** Create `app/Services/ModuleService.php` with Redis-cached module checks
- [ ] **2.6** Create `tenant()` global helper function returning `app('tenant')`
- [ ] **2.7** Create `module($key)` global helper returning `ModuleService::isEnabled($key)`
- [ ] **2.8** Create `app/Helpers/helpers.php` and register in [composer.json](file:///Users/bien/Downloads/pisti-app/composer.json) autoload

**Verification:**
```bash
# Set up local /etc/hosts: 127.0.0.1 happychurch-ruiru.pisti.local
# Visit happychurch-ruiru.pisti.local/dashboard
# Confirm: config('app.tenant_id') == 1 in tinker or in a debug route
```

