## Part 5: Delivery Timeline Summary

| Phase | Focus | Duration |
|-------|-------|----------|
| 0 | Infrastructure (Redis, Horizon, SSL, Nginx, Staging) | Days 1–3 |
| 1 | Core SaaS tables (tenants, plans, subscriptions, modules) | Days 4–7 |
| 2 | Tenant resolution middleware + module service | Days 7–9 |
| 3 | BelongsToTenant trait + critical models (users, settings) | Days 9–12 |
| 4 | Full 70-table migration + raw query audit | Days 12–18 |
| 5 | Module-gated routes + Blade UI guards | Days 18–22 |
| 6 | Integration isolation (Mpesa, SMS, Email, Storage, Jobs) | Days 22–26 |
| 7 | Billing & subscriptions | Days 26–33 |
| 8 | Superadmin panel | Days 33–40 |
| 9 | Tenant onboarding & self-service | Days 40–46 |
| 10 | Testing, security audit, production migration & launch | Days 46–55 |

**Total estimated duration: ~8 weeks**

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Phase 4 (full table migration) is the highest-risk phase. All 70 tables must have `tenant_id` before any phase 5+ work begins. Each batch should be migrated on the staging environment first and tested for data isolation before running on production.

> [!NOTE]
> The existing [MULTITENANT_SAAS_PLAN.md](file:///Users/bien/Downloads/pisti-app/MULTITENANT_SAAS_PLAN.md) is an excellent foundation and structurally sound. This plan extends it with the modular feature system, fixes the identified gaps, and provides execution-level granularity. The two plans should be considered complementary.
